{
  "id": "ep069",
  "duration": 49.921,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.525,
      "text": "A spacecraft designed to die in thirty-two minutes lasted two hours.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Venera 9 Space Probe 01.jpg",
        "credit": "Stolbovsky",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Venera_9_Space_Probe_01.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 1.7,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 1.7,
          "end": 4.533,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.525,
      "end": 12.12,
      "text": "On March 1, 1982, the Soviet Union's Venera 13 lander plunged into the atmosphere of Venus.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.533,
          "end": 12.133,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 12.12,
      "end": 18.415,
      "text": "It faced ninety atmospheres of pressure and temperatures near four hundred sixty degrees Celsius.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Venus as captured by Mariner 10 (cropped).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Venus_as_captured_by_Mariner_10_(cropped).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 12.133,
          "end": 16.033,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 16.033,
          "end": 18.4,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 18.415,
      "end": 24.96,
      "text": "The probe drilled for soil samples and captured the first color photographs ever taken on another planet.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "V13 vg261 262.tif",
        "credit": "USSR/NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:V13_vg261_262.tif"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 18.4,
          "end": 24.967,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 24.96,
      "end": 30.93,
      "text": "These images showed a jagged orange landscape littered with rocks and discarded lens caps.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Surface of Venus from Venera 13.jpg",
        "credit": "Lunar and Planetary Institute from Houston, TX, USA",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Surface_of_Venus_from_Venera_13.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 24.967,
          "end": 30.933,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 30.93,
      "end": 36.8,
      "text": "Years later, a scientist claimed the photos showed a moving alien shaped like a scorpion.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Surfaces of Venus, Venere 13 and Venera14.jpg",
        "credit": "Lunar and Planetary Institute from Houston, TX, USA",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Surfaces_of_Venus,_Venere_13_and_Venera14.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 30.933,
          "end": 34.6,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 34.6,
          "end": 36.8,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 36.8,
      "end": 42.2,
      "text": "Experts proved the alien was actually a lens cap that fell off during landing.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 36.8,
          "end": 42.2,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 42.2,
      "end": 49.571,
      "text": "Soviet engineers celebrated this machine, which was much more than just a spacecraft designed to die in thirty-two minutes.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Venera 9 Space Probe 01.jpg",
        "credit": "Stolbovsky",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Venera_9_Space_Probe_01.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 42.2,
          "end": 49.933,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
